    {
      "id": "s7",
      "caption": "Misconception: all acids are strong",
      "duration_ms": 6000,
      "narration": "Not every acid is fierce. Weak acids like vinegar only partly release their H+ ions. And pH measures the solution — how concentrated the ions are — not just which acid you started with.",
      "steps": [
